{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>לֵאמֹר בֹּא דַבֵּר וְגוֹ׳.</b> Its saying <b>לֵאמֹר</b> means that he should say to him, for He said to him בֹּא דַבֵּר, and His saying <b>וִישַׁלַּח</b> with the addition of the vav, even though nothing had preceded it, is because the mission of Moshe to speak to Pharaoh is a momentous matter — for a commoner to speak before a king — and moreover that he should speak to him things that pierce his heart, to extract 'בָּלְעוֹ' from his mouth." "<b>Further,</b> it intends to say to him that not only if they depart of their own accord will he not hinder them, but rather he himself must send them out as well and say to them ״קוּמוּ צְּאוּ״. Further, it intends that He is promising him that he shall speak, and assuredly that he will send them, and so forth, in the end."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:25:09.626169571Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}